  "claim": "Murabaḥah is a term for a sales contract where the buyer and seller agree on the markup, the ratio between the quality of a good or service and its selling price.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Murabaha. Sentence: Murabaḥah, murabaḥa or murâbaḥah (Arabic: مرابحة‎ ‎ , derived from \"ribh\" Arabic: ربح‎ ‎ , meaning profit) is a term of \"fiqh\" (Islamic jurisprudence) for a sales contract where the buyer and seller agree on the markup (profit) or \"cost-plus\" price for the item(s) being sold.\nPage: Markup (business). Sentence: Markup is the ratio between the cost of a good or service and its selling price.",
